page("who-a-collapsible-grill-suits","Who a Collapsible Charcoal Grill Suits (and Who It Doesn't)","An honest look at who gets the most from a flat-pack charcoal grill: campers, tailgaters, small-space cooks, hunters and more.","both02",f"""
<p>A collapsible charcoal grill is a specific tool. It's ideal for some cooks and the wrong choice for others.</p>
<h2>Good fit</h2>{table(["Who","Why it works"],[["Car campers and overlanders","Packs flat with the gear; burns charcoal or wood"],["Tailgaters","Flat pack in the trunk, sets up quickly"],["Apartment and small-home cooks","Stores on a shelf or behind a door (check your building's grill rules)"],["Hunters and anglers","Goes in the truck, UTV or camp box"],["Paddlers","The Compact packs about 1&quot; thick for a kayak or canoe (cook on shore, never on the boat)"],["Anyone who likes cooking over real fire","Charcoal and wood, direct heat, griddle option"]])}
<h2>Probably not the right fit</h2>{ul(["You want long, lidded low-and-slow cooks every weekend.","You want push-button heat with no fire to manage.","You can't commit to oiling carbon steel and storing it dry."])}
<h2>Picking a size</h2><p>The Slot Grill makers say the Compact is sized for one to three people, while the Full Size suits a family or group and bigger cuts. See {L("sizing-a-collapsible-grill-for-your-group","sizing for your group")} and {L("compact-vs-full-size-slot-grill","Compact vs Full Size")}.</p>
""","choosing",[])

page("collapsible-grill-buying-checklist","Collapsible Grill Buying Checklist","What to check before you buy a collapsible charcoal grill: steel thickness, packed size, setup, airflow, cooking area and where it's made.","c07",f"""
<p>Use this checklist on any collapsible grill. Answers for the Slot Grill are from SlotGrill.com.</p>
{table(["Check","Why it matters","Slot Grill"],[["Steel type and thickness","Thin steel warps and flexes","Carbon steel: 12-gauge Compact, 10-gauge Full Size"],["Packed thickness","Where it'll actually fit","About 1&quot; Compact, about 1.25&quot; Full Size"],["Weight","Carry distance","About 14 lb Compact, about 27.6 lb Full Size (grill only)"],["Setup","Tools, hinges, small parts","Tab and slot, no tools, no hinges, about 30–60 seconds"],["Cooking area","How many people","16.25&quot; × 9&quot; Compact; 20.5&quot; × 11.25&quot; Full Size"],["Airflow / elevation","Fire health and heat below","2⅞&quot; Compact, 3⅝&quot; Full Size air gap"],["Fuel","Flexibility","Charcoal or cooking wood"],["Accessories","Versatility","Griddle (plancha) plates, 1 or 2"],["Where it's made","Support and build quality","Made in the USA (Texas)"]])}
<h2>Buy from the source</h2><p>Slot Grill says it has no authorized third-party resellers and sells only at <a href="{HOME}">SlotGrill.com</a>, the @SlotGrill TikTok Shop and @SlotGrill on the Shop app. See {L("where-to-buy-a-genuine-slot-grill","where to buy a genuine Slot Grill")}.</p>
""","choosing",[])

page("sizing-a-collapsible-grill-for-your-group","Sizing a Collapsible Grill for Your Group","How much cooking area you need for one, two, four or a crowd, and how to cook in batches on a smaller grill.","full13",f"""
<p>Cooking area is the number that decides how many people you can feed at once. Here's how the two Slot Grills compare:</p>
{table(["","Compact","Full Size"],[["Cooking area","16.25&quot; × 9&quot; (146 sq in)","20.5&quot; × 11.25&quot; (231 sq in)"],["Slot Grill says","Sized for one to three people","Room for big cuts, cast iron and a full family cook"]])}
<h2>Rules of thumb</h2>{ul(["Leave a cool zone: count only about two-thirds of the grill for direct cooking.","Burgers: roughly 4 to 6 standard patties fit on the Compact at once; more on the Full Size. Exact count depends on patty size and how much cool zone you keep.","Groups bigger than the grill: cook in waves and hold finished food on the cool side or in a covered pan."])}
<h2>Cooking for a crowd</h2><p>Prep everything before lighting, cook in order (vegetables, then meat), and keep a second chimney going for fresh coals. Or bring both sizes.</p>
""","choosing",[])

page("compact-vs-full-size-slot-grill","Compact vs Full Size Slot Grill: Which Collapsible Grill Fits You?","A side-by-side comparison of the Slot Grill Compact and Full Size: steel, weight, cooking area, air gap, packed size and price, from SlotGrill.com.","both16",f"""
<p>Both Slot Grills share the same tab-and-slot design. Slot Grill describes the Compact as the same design at 80% scale. The differences come down to size, steel thickness and weight. All figures below are from SlotGrill.com.</p>
{table(["","Compact","Full Size"],[["Steel","12-gauge carbon steel","10-gauge carbon steel"],["Footprint","17.5&quot; × 10.25&quot; (179 sq in)","21.75&quot; × 12.75&quot; (277 sq in)"],["Cooking area","16.25&quot; × 9&quot; (146 sq in)","20.5&quot; × 11.25&quot; (231 sq in)"],["Height","10.5&quot;","13&quot;"],["Air gap","2⅞&quot;","3⅝&quot;"],["Packed thickness","About 1&quot;","About 1.25&quot;"],["Weight (grill only)","About 14 lb","About 27.6 lb"],["With 1 / 2 griddles","16.2 / 18.4 lb","31.8 / 36.4 lb"],["Setup","Tab and slot, no tools, about 30–60 seconds","Same"],["Fuel","Charcoal or cooking wood","Same"],["Price (grill only)","$89.97","$149.97"]])}
<h2>Choose the Compact if</h2>{ul(["You cook for one to three people.","You carry it any distance, or pack a trunk, kayak or camp box.","You want the lightest heavy-duty option."])}
<h2>Choose the Full Size if</h2>{ul(["You cook for a family or a group.","You want room for cast iron and bigger cuts.","You travel by truck, UTV, RV or boat, where the weight is no problem."])}
<h2>Griddle either way</h2><p>Both take one or two <a href="{GRID}">griddle plates</a>. Grill-plus-griddle bundles are listed on each product page.</p>
""","choosing",[("Which Slot Grill is lighter?","The Compact, at about 14 lb versus about 27.6 lb for the Full Size (grill only).")])

page("collapsible-grill-for-small-spaces","Collapsible Grills for Small Spaces: Patios, Balconies and Small Yards","How a flat-pack charcoal grill can work for small outdoor spaces, plus the rules and safety checks to make first.","c07",f"""
<p>A grill that stores flat is appealing when you don't have room for a permanent cooker. But small spaces come with rules.</p>
<h2>Check first</h2>{ul(["<b>Rules.</b> Many apartment buildings, condos and local fire codes restrict charcoal grills on balconies or near buildings. Check your lease, HOA and local fire code before you buy or light anything.","<b>Surface.</b> Non-combustible only: concrete, pavers, gravel. Not a wood deck or plastic tiles.","<b>Clearance.</b> Away from walls, railings, overhangs, furniture and plants."])}
<h2>Making it work</h2>{ul(["Store it flat indoors so it doesn't rust on the patio.","Use the Compact for a small spot; 17.5&quot; × 10.25&quot; footprint.","Light with a chimney to avoid lighter fluid smell near neighbors.","Have a plan for ash: a lidded metal can."])}
""","choosing",[])
